MathCAT (LaTeX braille code): plain LaTeX, written again as LaTeX builds it

Mathessible writes a LaTeX document's equations from their MathML with
MathCAT's LaTeX braille code (an edit in the professional view, a paste,
a document changed to LaTeX), and that LaTeX is built again by
UnicodeMathML's TeX2UnicodeMath. What the code wrote did not always build
back, or was no LaTeX:

- The "ct:"/"tc:" concatenation markers (U+F8FE, U+F8FF) of the unicode
  tables were left in the output (around \mathbf v, before Greek
  letters): LaTeX_cleanup removes them, as speech does.
- Math italic Greek wrote \mathmit, no LaTeX command: lowercase italic
  Greek is LaTeX's own \alpha; capitals are \mathit\Gamma; \mathmit{\nabla}
  and the like are \nabla.
- A function name's limits (lim, max, sup, ...) were \underset{x \to 0}{\lim}:
  they are now \lim_{x \to 0}, as the large operators' are.
- The converter's combining accents (U+20D7, U+0303, ...) were
  \overset{\vec}{v}: they are now accents, \vec{v} and \tilde{z}.
- cases (a "{" before a table, with no closing fence) lost its structure:
  \begin{cases} ... \end{cases}.
- Text (mtext) was written as math letters: \text{...}, its spaces kept
  as spaces (not \space or \~, which are for math).
- A table with no fence before it was bare rows: aligned equations
  (intent :equations) are \begin{aligned} ... \end{aligned}, others
  \begin{matrix} ... \end{matrix}.
- A name of several letters applied as a function (U+2061 after it, as
  Mathessible builds \DeclareMathOperator{\tr}{tr}) lost its name: trA.
  It is \operatorname{tr}A, its scripts after it.
- The math alphabets' epsilon symbol (italic U+1D716, as the converter
  builds \epsilon, and its bold, sans and bold italic forms) was written
  \in, the element-of sign; bold and sans bold were \varepsilon. They
  are \epsilon.
- The math alphabets were written with commands LaTeX lacks (unicode-math
  and older names): \mathbit, \mathsfbf, \mathsfbfsl, \mathsfsl,
  \mathbcal, \mathbfrak, \mscrH, \mfrakH, \Planckconst for the italic h
  every h is built as, and Greek capitals \Alpha, \Beta, \Rho, \M, \N,
  \O (which is Ø) and lowercase \o (ø) for omicron. They are amsmath's
  and amssymb's: \boldsymbol{x}, \boldsymbol{\mathcal{L}},
  \boldsymbol{\mathsf{A}}, \mathcal H, h, A, B, P, M, N, O, o. Sans
  italic is \mathsf (LaTeX has no sans italic math).
- Table faults: double-struck letters were \mathbb only with short names
  (else a bare letter); the capital theta symbols were missing from the
  translate lists (the bold one held a reserved code), so the letters
  after them were shifted (Θ written \Sigma); 𝝰 fell in the range before
  its own and had no letter; the double-struck zero's list held a plain
  0; the four "tc: W" wrote a letter W for the space marker; italic
  capital Greek ran \mathit into the letter (\mathitA); dotless i and j
  and the bold digammas had no entry.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of upstream 85c89a37. Each is a bug
in the LaTeX code itself, for braille readers too; worth proposing upstream.

diff --git a/Rules/Braille/LaTeX/LaTeX_Rules.yaml b/Rules/Braille/LaTeX/LaTeX_Rules.yaml
index b9237dee..820b4a1b 100644
--- a/Rules/Braille/LaTeX/LaTeX_Rules.yaml
+++ b/Rules/Braille/LaTeX/LaTeX_Rules.yaml
@@ -102,6 +102,31 @@
   - x: "string($MatrixType)"     # need to get $MatrixType eval'd so that it is converted to braille (doesn't work if I do it in 'variables') 
   - t: "}𝐖"
 
+-
+  name: cases
+  tag: mrow
+  match: "*[1][.='{'] and *[2][self::m:mtable] and (count(*)=2 or count(*)=3 and *[3][self::m:mo and normalize-space(translate(., '​', ''))=''])"
+  replace:
+  - t: "𝐖\\begin{cases}𝐖"
+  - x: "*[2]"
+  - t: "𝐖\\end{cases}𝐖"
+
+-
+  # a table with no fence before it (cases and matrices have theirs): aligned equations or a matrix
+  name: unfenced-mtable
+  tag: mtable
+  match: "not(preceding-sibling::*)"
+  variables:
+  - TableType: "IfThenElse(contains(@intent, 'equations'), 'aligned', 'matrix')"
+  replace:
+  - t: "𝐖\\begin{"
+  - x: "string($TableType)"
+  - t: "}𝐖"
+  - x: "*"
+  - t: "𝐖\\end{"
+  - x: "string($TableType)"
+  - t: "}𝐖"
+
 -
   name: default-mtable
   tag: mtable
@@ -213,6 +238,29 @@
   - x: "text()"
   - t: "𝐖"
     
+-
+  # A name of several letters applied as a function (`\DeclareMathOperator`): `\operatorname{tr}`.
+  name: operator-name
+  tag: [mi, mtext]
+  match:
+  - "string-length(.) > 1 and"
+  - "( following-sibling::*[1][self::m:mo and .='⁡'] or"
+  - "  (parent::m:msub or parent::m:msup or parent::m:msubsup) and not(preceding-sibling::*) and"
+  - "    ../following-sibling::*[1][self::m:mo and .='⁡'] )"
+  replace:
+  - t: "\\operatorname{"
+  - x: "text()"
+  - t: "}"
+
+-
+  name: text
+  tag: mtext
+  match: "."
+  replace:
+  - t: "\\text{"
+  - x: "text()"
+  - t: "}"
+
 -
   # FIX: need to deal with all caps
   name: default
@@ -336,7 +384,8 @@
 -
   name: "movable-limits"
   tag: [munder, mover, munderover]
-  match: "*[1][IsInDefinition(., 'Braille', 'MovableLimitsLargeOps') or @movablelimits='true']"
+  match: "*[1][IsInDefinition(., 'Braille', 'MovableLimitsLargeOps') or @movablelimits='true' or
